<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Extinguish</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>extinguish &lt;torch or lantern&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>extinguish torch
</pre>
<p>Puts out a burning torch, lantern or other light, to save what is left of 
it for later: a light burns for so many hours, and then it is used up. 
Light it again with <a cmd='#'>Help Light</a>. It works on lights you carry and on 
lights lying in the room.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Light</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Torch</a>
</pre>




</div>